First-party implementation and provenance

The maintainer confirms that Rudroid was written as a new Rust implementation,
with Bogodroid's C++ tree used as a behavioral reference. It is not linked into
or distributed as Rudroid's runtime. The workspace was initially developed in
that local tree and moved here on 2026-10-09; the directory history alone does
not determine the copyright ownership of an independent implementation.

The maintainer-owned GLES sharp shader and offline resource tools were developed
in that local tree before reuse here. The shader's C++ history identifies
jenny92-tech as its author. Compatibility names, ABI constants and format rules
remain references, not assertions that Rudroid owns an upstream implementation.
This notice does not claim rights over Bogodroid's C++ code or other contributors'
work, or grant permission to relicense such material.

Third-party exceptions

- crates/capability/android/bionic/src/jump.S adapts AOSP's ARM64 setjmp code.
  Its original BSD-2-Clause notice is retained in the file and reproduced in
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES for binary distribution.
- crates/capability/android/jni_vm/tests/fixtures/jni.h is an AOSP test header,
  copied via Bogodroid/libjnivm/include/jni.h. Its Apache-2.0 notice is retained;
  provenance is documented beside it in JNI-ORIGIN.md.
- THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES records exact locked Rust dependency versions, registry
  checksums and original license texts. Include it with binaries.
- Optional WSI, Vulkan-Headers and Wayland protocol sources carry their own
  licenses and source receipt in vulkan-wsi/. The linked first-party Rust
  allocator uses Rudroid's root LICENSE; upstream components keep their terms.
- Host libraries, games/assets and companion launchers have separate licenses.

